@nsobid-D824D4B1BBD45D03668380D6D041BA4CA00A64FF

# The Legend of Zelda: Skyward Sword HD [01002DA013484000] v1.0.0 - 4:3
#
# EXPERIMENTAL -- unlike the Hyrule Warriors patch, this one is inferred.
# No aspect-ratio mod exists for this game, so there is no known-good 16:9
# constant to rewrite. Instead this narrows the render target to a 4:3 shape
# and relies on the game deriving its aspect from that.
#
# If the game does derive it, you get true 4:3. If it hard-codes 16:9 instead,
# you will get a squished picture -- in which case this route does not work for
# this game and the patch should be removed. Check a round object to tell.
#
# Only the WIDTHS are changed. Every height is left at stock, so vertical
# detail is untouched and the narrower frame is cheaper to render:
#
#   docked    1920 x 1080  ->  1440 x 1080
#   handheld  1280 x  720  ->   960 x  720
#
# Offsets are theboy181's, from their 2K and 4K resolution mods for this same
# build (https://github.com/theboy181/switch-ptchtxt-mods). Those mods write a
# (width, height) u32 pair at each address, and MOVZ W8 immediates at 00EC803C
# (width) and 00EC8068 (height). This writes only the width half of each.
#
# Pair this with Eden: Aspect Ratio -> Force 4:3.

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// docked render width 1920 -> 1440, height left at 1080
@enabled
016CAC94 A0050000
013A916C A0050000

// the same width set as a MOVZ W8 immediate: MOVZ W8, #1440
00EC803C 08B48052

// handheld render width 1280 -> 960, height left at 720
013A915C C0030000
@stop

# Note: theboy181's 4K mod also touches 013A9164, a third entry in the same
# resolution table. Its stock height is unknown, so it is deliberately left
# alone here. If the picture is right in one mode but not the other, that entry
# is the first thing to look at.
